      "raw_response": " ANSWER: SUPPORTED\n\nThe abstract presents a new technique for high-resolution in vivo imaging of myelinated axons, which allows for the observation of nodes of Ranvier and Schmidt-Lanterman incisures (structures associated with myelin sheaths). The method's ability to capture de novo myelination of mouse cortical axons in vivo (live animals) and the potential imaging of myelinated axons in the human cerebral cortex suggests that myelin sheaths indeed play a role in action potential propagation, as action potentials are involved in the transmission of electrical signals along neurons, and myelin sheaths are critical for the efficient conduction of these signals.",
