      "raw_response": "This abstract supports the claim that myelin sheaths play a role in action potential propagation. The technique described allows for the imaging of myelinated axons and the observation of nodes of Ranvier, which are critical structures for the propagation of action potentials along the axon. The fact that this technique is able to capture de novo myelination and image myelinated axons in the human cerebral cortex also suggests that myelin sheaths are essential for the function of the nervous system.\n\nANSWER: SUPPORTED",
